>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (Our goal was threefold: first, to anticipate electricity consumption peaks so that energy supply contracts can be negotiated more advantageously; second, to detect abnormal consumption patterns automatically that might signal a technical malfunction or an ongoing waste; and third, to support budget allocation decisions for each facility manager with reliable forecasts grounded in historical data.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (To achieve this, we designed and implemented a complete Big Data processing chain on the HDP 3.0 platform, covering every step from raw data ingestion to the delivery of a trained predictive model. The technical stack relies on Apache Hive for structured data warehousing, Apache Spark for distributed in-memory processing, and Spark MLlib for predictive modeling. All Spark code was developed inside Apache Zeppelin notebooks as required.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (This report walks through each stage of that pipeline. Section 2 describes the data warehouse architecture built in Hive. Section 3 covers the Spark processing pipeline. Section 4 presents the machine learning pipeline and its results. Section 5 provides a critical analysis of those results, and Section 6 concludes with concrete improvement proposals.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
